# Ensure consistent LF line endings for KCL test data across platforms.
# Without this, Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` converts LF to CRLF
# on checkout, which causes the KCL formatter to rewrite the file (seen
# as a change in `test_format_path_api`).
#
# `*.k` covers every language's test fixture (nodejs/__test__/test_data,
# go/test_data, python/tests/test_data, java/src/test_data,
# kotlin/src/test_data, dotnet/KclLib.Tests/test_data, cpp/test_data,
# swift/test_data, ruby/test_data, lua/spec/test_data, plus the top-level
# testdata/) so the formatter sees LF on Windows CI just like on macOS/Linux.
*.k text eol=lf
python/tests/test_data/** text eol=lf